## Review: issue #45 — Make delayed navigation in SessionCompleteScreen explicit and cancellable

## Findings

No code-review findings in the current revision.

`SessionCompleteScreen`'s auto-advance now uses an owned `Timer` instead of
an uncancelled `Future.delayed`. `_continue()` cancels the timer before
acting (rather than relying on `mounted` alone), and `dispose()` cancels it
too, so it can never fire after the screen leaves the tree. A `_hasAdvanced`
flag added during an earlier local review pass (an in-house `/code-review`
run flagged that `mounted` alone doesn't stop `_continue()` from being
re-entered by a second manual invocation, e.g. a double-tap, while the
push-replacement transition is still in flight) makes the navigation
idempotent regardless of what triggers it.

